# HTTP routes — central catalog

All API URL registration lives in **[`backend/src/http/route.js`](backend/src/http/route.js)**.
Do **not** add per-resource `*Routes` plugins. Resource files export named `*Http`
adapters; `route.js` wires method, path, access, and handler.

Mounted under `API_BASE_PATH` from `http/app.js`. Root `/health` and `/readiness`
reuse the same health handlers outside the catalog plugin.

## Path shape

Product paths:

```text
/{module}/{file}/{action}
/{module}/{file}/{action}/:ids…   # GET (and HEAD) only
```

Examples: `/masters/users/create`, `POST /conversation/conversation/restore` (ids in body),
`GET /conversation/conversation/get/:projectId/:conversationId`.

- **module** — one of `access`, `masters`, `knowledge`, `conversation` (or `http` for probes).
- **file** — resource file stem (`users`, `auth`, `repositories`, …).
- **action** — product verb matching the handler (`create`, `list`, `restore`, …).
- **Mutating methods** (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) — no resource ids in the path; put every
  id in the JSON body (multipart text fields for upload). Project ACL reads `projectId`
  from the body on those methods.
- **GET** may keep `:ids` in the path; project ACL reads `projectId` from params.
- **Health** stays flat: `/health`, `/readiness` (also registered at process root).

Do not invent alternate path layouts without an explicit product decision.

## Handlers (`*Http`)

- Live in the owning resource file; re-export from the module `index.js`.
- Names are **product verbs**, not HTTP methods: `createConversationHttp`,
  `restoreConversationHttp`, `listUsersHttp`, `loginHttp` — **not**
  `postConversationRestoreHttp` / `getUsersHttp`.
- Keep service/repository function names unchanged (`createConversation`, …).
- The `*Http` adapter owns request validation and `reply`; it calls the service and
  does not pass `reply` into helpers (`function-design.mdc`).

## Access helpers (call sites stay positional)

Use the helpers in `route.js` — **no options objects** at registration call sites:

| Helper | Purpose |
| ------ | ------- |
| `withPublicAccess(requireCsrf?)` | Public; `true` attaches CSRF from the app |
| `withAuthenticatedAccess(allowWhenMustChangePassword?, requireIdempotencyKey?)` | Authenticated, no project ACL |
| `withRequiredPermissions(permission(s), requireIdempotencyKey?)` | Org `requiredPermissions` |
| `withProjectAccess(permission(s), requireIdempotencyKey?, consumeSourceArchive?)` | Authenticated + project ACL preHandler |

`withProjectAccess`: a **string** permission uses mode `all`; an **array** always means
**any** (do not pass a `mode` argument).

```js
// ❌ BAD
app.post('/…', { config: { requiredPermissions: ['users.manage'] } }, createUserHttp);
app.get('/…', withProjectAccess(preHandler), getProjectHttp);
app.post('/…', withPublicAccess(app.csrfProtection), refreshSessionHttp);

// ✅ GOOD
app.post('/masters/users/create', withRequiredPermissions('users.manage', true), createUserHttp);
app.post('/masters/projects/archive', withProjectAccess('projects.update'), archiveProjectHttp);
app.get('/masters/projects/get/:projectId', withProjectAccess('projects.view'), getProjectHttp);
app.post('/access/auth/refresh', withPublicAccess(true), refreshSessionHttp);
app.get('/…', withProjectAccess(['knowledge.browse', 'knowledge.view']), getKnowledgeSummaryHttp);
```

## Catalog comments

In `registerRoutes`:

- **Module** start/end only — banner comments:

```js
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// masters
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// …routes…
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// end masters
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

- **Resource file** — one line: `// users.js`

Do not put a full banner on every file.

## Adding a route

1. Add or reuse an `*Http` export on the resource file (product-language name + JSDoc).
2. Export it from the module `index.js` if callers use the barrel.
3. Register it in `route.js` under the correct module/file section with the path shape above
   and the matching access helper.
4. Cover unhappy paths in tests (`backend/tests/…`); keep the route-declaration audit green.

## Forbidden

- New `*Routes` / `identityRoutes` Fastify plugins that call `app.get` / `app.post`
- Registering domain URLs outside `http/route.js` (except root health aliases in `app.js`)
- HTTP-method prefixes in handler names (`post…Http`, `get…Http`, `patch…Http`)
- Options-object bags on access helpers at catalog call sites
